HORUS v@PROJECT_VERSION@ makes repeat case triage easier to review and PE comparisons easier to automate.

Highlights:

- Each case refresh records what changed in the current run: added, modified, restored, missing, removed by `--prune`, and assessment-changed samples. Review the `changes` array and `summary.changes` in `case.json`, the new `changes.csv`, or the offline dashboard.
- The feed covers the latest refresh, not a historical audit log. Use `--verify` to detect edits that preserve both file size and modification time.
- `horus --diff a.exe b.exe --json` provides a machine-readable PE comparison. Incomplete or non-PE comparisons set `analysis_status` to `unknown` and exit 3 instead of implying a complete PE comparison.
- Malformed PE input handling and CLI mode validation are stricter.
- The established direct-file, case, and opt-in enrichment workflows remain available. Samples are never uploaded by HORUS.

The three binaries target Windows 10/11 x64. They are not Authenticode-signed; verify downloads with `SHA256SUMS.txt` and GitHub artifact attestations.
